 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Partial Occlusion Artifacts:** If a cube touches a slab, the slab's side is culled, but the cube's side remains half-visible. The engine leaves triangles of the whole side visible, as sides are either fully culled or not culled [S1].
-*   **Transparency Issues:** Transparency exposes underlying geometry due to culling limitations. There is no way to avoid this other than avoiding such situations in game design (e.g., no glass slabs in Minecraft) [S1].
